CLASS:: SwarmPlayback
summary:: Apply an event and wait on the caller's clock using borrowed registry playback
categories:: Libraries>SwarmSynth
related:: Classes/SwarmInstrumentRegistry, Classes/SwarmMath, Classes/SwarmSynth

DESCRIPTION::
SwarmPlayback is a synchronous scheduling helper for composition code. It resolves one raw registry binding, applies an Event to that state, updates the resolved synth, and yields for a separate number of beats. It creates no Routine and uses the caller's clock.

The resolved state and synth are borrowed. SwarmPlayback does not create, reset, release, or dispose playback. In particular, it deliberately bypasses code::SwarmInstrument.play:: so a code::\nextTrigger:: registration does not reset production nodes. If the registry binding changes while the caller is waiting, optional gate closure still targets the synth resolved at the start of the call.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: play
Applies an event, waits, optionally closes the resolved synth's gate, and returns the Event produced by code::registry.at(name)::.

argument:: registry
A SwarmInstrumentRegistry, or another object implementing code::at(name):: with the same raw-binding contract.

argument:: name
The registered instrument name.

argument:: event
The Event passed to code::state.putEvent::. Envelope duration remains an explicit event value and is independent from code::waitBeats::.

argument:: waitBeats
A nonnegative finite number yielded to the caller's Routine. It is validated before registry lookup or state mutation.

argument:: closeGate
When exactly code::true::, calls code::closeGate:: on the synth resolved before the wait. The default is false.

argument:: excludeParams
Optional parameter names forwarded unchanged to code::synth.set(state, excludeParams: excludeParams)::.

EXAMPLES::

code::
Routine {
    // A short envelope may be followed by a longer scheduled rest.
    SwarmPlayback.play(
        ~registry, \bell,
        (midinote: 64, duration: 0.25),
        waitBeats: 1,
        closeGate: true,
        excludeParams: [\phase, \pan]
    );
}.play(TempoClock.default);
::
